                <pb facs="1345" n="1335" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1335"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/9–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-11T12:00:00+08:00">September 11,
                            1949—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 12—11:29 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 1086. Chen Tai-chu, Director American Section FonOff, said Nationalist
                    Government has no objection to through passengers on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi> (telCan 649, September 3, repeated Shanghai 1799). He
                    reiterated, however, his Government’s objection to booking passengers to
                    Shanghai from Hong Kong or elsewhere.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Shanghai 531.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
